title: CricketDada_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Emotional_2>>
<<SetBGSprite SurakshaHospital>>

// Scene Setup - Hospital visit
While running errands near the local hospital, Raju hears cricket commentary echoing from one of the rooms. His curiosity draws him in.

The hospital corridors seem less intimidating as cricket commentary echoes ahead. Raju's footsteps guide him toward the familiar sound.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Ah, beta! Another cricket lover, I see.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: I heard the commentary from outside. Who's playing?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: It's an old match recording. Vishwanath just played a classic cover drive.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: A cover drive? That's one of the most elegant shots!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: The kind they don't teach anymore, beta. You know your cricket!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: You talk about Vishwanath like you've seen him play many times.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Beta, I've been following cricket for fifty years.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Fifty years! You must have seen so many legends!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Kapil Dev's World Cup victory, Gavaskar's determination, Vishwanath's elegance. Each generation brings new heroes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: But how do you remember so many details from decades ago?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: When you love something truly, every moment becomes precious.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: I remember Kapil Dev's catch in 1983 like it happened yesterday. That catch changed everything.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: The one that dismissed Viv Richards? I've read about that!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: You're well-read for a young boy. Tell me, who's your favorite player?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I love watching the current team, but hearing you talk about the legends makes me want to learn more.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: That's the spirit, beta. History teaches us where we came from.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Do you watch all the matches alone, Dada?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: These days, yes. But cricket is good company.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Don't your family members visit to watch with you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: Family... well, cricket is enough company for an old man.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: These young cricketers today play with such fire. Like you, beta - I can see the passion in your eyes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Thank you, Dada. Can I visit you again?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: I would like that very much, beta. Very much indeed.

<<HideCharacter>>

// Scene Conclusion
As Raju leaves, Cricket Dada's stories echo in his mind. The elderly man's passion is inspiring, but his loneliness is concerning.

<<set $CricketDada_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: CricketDada_Day2
tags: 
position: -7,-50
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Emotional_2>>
<<SetBGSprite SurakshaHospital>>

// Scene Setup - Day 2
Eager to continue yesterday's conversation, Raju returns after school. He brings a notebook to record the incredible stories.

The hospital feels more familiar today. Raju's notebook represents his serious intention to preserve Cricket Dada's memories.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Ah, my young friend returns! I was hoping you would come back.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I couldn't stop thinking about your stories, Dada.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: I spent all night thinking of more stories to share with you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I brought this notebook to write everything down.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I want to remember the matches, the players, all the special moments.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Very good, beta. Cricket history should be preserved.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Passed from generation to generation. Let me tell you about the 1971 series.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Against which team?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: The West Indies! They were giants, beta. We were underdogs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But we won, didn't we?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: We drew the series. But we proved we could stand tall against anyone.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Dada, you talk about cricket like it teaches life lessons, not just sports.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Exactly! Cricket is life, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Every match teaches you about facing challenges, working with others.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: When Kapil Dev led us to World Cup victory, they proved determination can overcome any disadvantage.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: So cricket is more than just a game?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Cricket mirrors life's most important battles.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Every bowler faces rejection. Every batsman faces failure. Every team faces impossible odds.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Serious">>
Cricket Dada: How you respond defines your character, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's exactly what I feel when I play!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Cricket teaches me to be stronger, to handle pressure, to never give up.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: You understand it well for someone so young.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Quizzical">>
Cricket Dada: Tell me about your cricket dreams, beta. What drives your passion?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I dream of playing for my school team one day.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: But more than that, I want to understand cricket the way you do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Keep that fire burning, beta. The game needs passionate players like you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I'll come back tomorrow, Dada. I want to hear more stories.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: I'll be waiting, beta. I'll be waiting.

<<HideCharacter>>

// Scene Conclusion
Raju's notebook fills with cricket wisdom. Cricket Dada has become more than a storyteller - he's becoming a mentor.

