// Scene Setup - Day 3
Raju brings a cricket magazine he bought with his lunch money. But today, something feels different about Cricket Dada.

The room carries different energy today. Raju detects a melancholy beneath Cricket Dada's usual enthusiasm.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I brought you this cricket magazine, Dada.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: It has articles about current players and some history sections.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: Beta, you didn't need to spend money on an old man.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: But this means more to me than you know.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: It's been so long since anyone thought to bring me something.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Dada, something is troubling you today. I can see it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: You're very perceptive, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Would you like to talk about it?

