title: CricketDada_Day3a
tags:
position: -308,129
---

<<set $CricketDada_Path = "a">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I can see you're sad, Dada. Sometimes sharing helps.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: Most people don't notice when old men are struggling inside.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: It's about loneliness, beta. About choices I made long ago.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'm here to listen, Dada. Take your time.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Sometimes the heart needs to speak as much as the mind needs to remember cricket stories.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: Your gentleness reminds me of my daughter Priya.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: She used to listen with the same patience you're showing now.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: She sounds wonderful, Dada. Where is she now?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Why isn't she here with you?

<<jump CricketDada_Day3_Continue>>
===

title: CricketDada_Day3b
tags:
position: -55,122
---

<<set $CricketDada_Path = "b">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Dada, I noticed the photo you tried to hide.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Are you missing your family?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: You don't miss much, do you beta?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: Yes, that photo is all I have left of happier times.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: What happened, Dada? Did you fight with them?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: I made mistakes, said things in anger.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: I felt like they didn't respect me anymore. That they saw me as a burden.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: So you stopped calling them?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: But Dada, maybe they're waiting for you to call? Someone has to make the first move.

<<jump CricketDada_Day3_Continue>>
===

title: CricketDada_Day3c
tags:
position: 184,122
---

<<set $CricketDada_Path = "c">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: The cricket heroes you tell me about - they faced lonely times too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: How did they handle it? What would Kapil Dev do?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Quizzical">>
Cricket Dada: That's an interesting way to think about it, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Serious">>
Cricket Dada: Kapil Dev never gave up, even when the odds seemed impossible.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: So what would he do with a family misunderstanding?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Would he wait for the other team to move, or would he take action?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Quizzical">>
Cricket Dada: He would be brave. He would take the risk.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Make the play that could win or lose everything. Just like in 1983.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Maybe it's time to be as brave as your cricket heroes, Dada.

<<jump CricketDada_Day3_Continue>>
===

title: CricketDada_Day3_Continue
tags:
---

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: That photo was taken fifteen years ago at a cricket match.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: My wife Kamala, my son Sunil, my daughter Priya.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: We used to attend matches together, listen to commentary at home.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Fifteen years? That's such a long time, Dada.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: They became busy with their own lives, their own families.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Sad">>
Cricket Dada: I convinced myself they were better off without their stubborn old father.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: But Dada, what if they think you abandoned them?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: What if they're waiting for you to reach out?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: All these years might have been a terrible misunderstanding.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Quizzical">>
Cricket Dada: What do you mean, beta?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: When I fight with my brother Ramu, we both wait for the other to apologize first.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: But someone has to make the first move, or we stay angry forever.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: The cricket heroes you admire - they never gave up when things looked impossible.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Quizzical">>
Cricket Dada: You think they might be waiting for me?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: All these years, I thought they abandoned me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: But what if they think I abandoned them?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Maybe it's time to be brave like the champions I've spent my life admiring.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Yes, Dada! Take the risk, like Kapil Dev did.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Beta, you've given this old man hope. Real hope.

<<HideCharacter>>

// Scene Conclusion
Raju leaves carrying the weight of Cricket Dada's revelation and hope that his advice might bridge fifteen years of separation.

