title: CricketDada_Day4
tags:
position: -7,75
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Emotional_2>>
<<SetBGSprite SurakshaHospital>>

// Scene Setup - Day 4
Curious whether Cricket Dada contacted his family, Raju makes what might be his final visit to the hospital.

The hospital buzzes with different energy today. Raju approaches with nervous anticipation about what he might find.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Beta! Come, come quickly!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Dada, you sound so excited! What happened?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Meet my family! They're here!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Kamala, Sunil, Priya - this is Raju, the young cricket enthusiast I told you about.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: The one who gave me the wisdom to call you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamala" "Smiling">>
Kamala: Raju, beta, we've heard so much about you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamala" "Sad">>
Kamala: My husband tells me you encouraged him to reach out to us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamala" "Smiling">>
Kamala: We were so afraid he didn't want to see us anymore.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: You were both waiting for the other to make the first move.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Just like I thought!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Sunil" "Smiling">>
Sunil: Fifteen years of missing each other because we were all too proud.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Sunil" "Excited">>
Sunil: It took a wise young boy to show us what cricket teaches.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Sunil" "Smiling">>
Sunil: Sometimes you have to take risks to win the match.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I just used the lessons Cricket Dada taught me about cricket and life.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Beta, you taught me something more valuable than any cricket statistic.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: You showed me that the best innings aren't played on the field.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: They're played in life, when you find the courage to rebuild what seemed broken.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Priya" "Smiling">>
Priya: Papa has told us so much about your cricket dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Priya" "Excited">>
Priya: He says you remind him of the champions he's watched over the decades.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Cricket Dada taught me that cricket and life follow the same rules.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Every champion faces impossible odds, but they win by staying focused.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: And never losing hope.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: And you taught me that wisdom flows both ways, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Sometimes the teacher learns the most important lesson from the student.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamala" "Smiling">>
Kamala: Raju, you must visit us at home. We'll watch a cricket match together.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Priya" "Excited">>
Priya: Yes! Papa can tell all of us his stories, just like old times.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I would love that! Thank you!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Smiling">>
Cricket Dada: Beta, you've given me my family back. I can never repay this gift.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: You've already given me so much, Dada. You taught me that cricket wisdom works everywhere.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: And you taught me to be brave, to take the winning shot even when afraid.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Sunil" "Smiling">>
Sunil: This calls for celebration! Let's all watch the match together.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CricketDada" "Excited">>
Cricket Dada: Yes! Just like the old days. Beta, sit next to me. I'll explain every shot.

<<HideCharacter>>

// Scene Conclusion
As the family gathers around the television, Raju witnesses the joy of reconciliation. Cricket Dada's transformation is complete - from lonely patient to surrounded patriarch.

